rate-of-energy-loss.conceptual_definition:
This formula quantifies the rate at which a system loses energy, specifically when that loss is proportional to the product of a characteristic quantity (represented by 
$\Omega$
) and its rate of change (represented by 
$\dot{\Omega}$
). This relationship is commonly observed in systems where energy dissipation is driven by changes in some dynamical variable or configuration parameter.
